@*
    Shared Task action dialogs -- Edit / Complete / Close / Add Evidence.

    Paired with wwwroot/js/Shared/task-actions.js (window.gracTaskActions),
    which is the ONLY code that opens, fills or submits these. Include
    this partial once on any page that wants those actions (Task Center's
    tasks.cshtml, Task View's task-view.cshtml), load task-actions.js,
    and call window.gracTaskActions.init({...}) once during that page's
    own init.

    Moved out of tasks.cshtml unchanged (change request: Task View's own
    "Actions" menu must reuse the exact same forms/modals Task Center's
    3-dot menu opens, not a second copy) so there is one markup source
    for every page that offers these actions.

    "Add Child Task" / "New Task" is NOT here -- that already had its own
    shared dialog before this change: Partials/_task-form-dialog.cshtml +
    Shared/task-form.js (window.gracTaskForm).
*@
@*
    Task View / Edit -- ONE dialog, two modes.

    View is the read-only representation of the task; Edit modifies it;
    Complete and Close are workflow actions with their own confirmations
    below. Keeping View and Edit in one dialog rather than two screens is
    deliberate: the reader who decides to edit is looking at the fields
    they want to change, and a second window would make them find their
    place again.

    The Edit button sits top-right, next to the close control, which is
    where a reader looks after finishing the page.
*@
<dialog id="taskDetailDialog" style="max-width:980px; width:94%;">
    @* The padding lives in CSS, not inline: edit mode needs to tighten it,
       and an inline style beats any selector. Same values as before for
       the read-only view. *@
    <div class="tdd-body">
        <div style="display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:flex-start; gap:12px; margin-bottom:12px;">
            <h2 id="taskDetailTitle" style="margin:0; font-size:17px;">Task</h2>
            <div style="display:flex; align-items:center; gap:8px; flex:0 0 auto;">
                @* Shown in view mode only; hidden while editing, because
                   an Edit button on an edit form is a dead control. *@
                <button type="button" id="taskDetailEditBtn" class="pm-button" hidden>
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-pen" aria-hidden="true"></i> Edit
                </button>
                <button type="button" id="taskDetailClose" aria-label="Close" style="background:none; border:none; font-size:20px; cursor:pointer; line-height:1;">&times;</button>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div id="taskDetailBody"></div>
    </div>
</dialog>

<style>
    /* Task edit form (269, carried over unchanged). Scoped to
       #taskEditForm, which exists only while the dialog is in edit mode,
       so none of this can reach the read-only view or any other form on
       the page. */

    /* WIDER ONLY WHILE EDITING.
       The form carries three columns of controls where the read-only view
       carries prose, so it needs the room -- but the View keeps the width
       it has always had. setDetailMode() toggles the class. */
    #taskDetailDialog.is-editing { max-width: 1180px; }

    /* Moved off the element's inline style so edit mode can override it —
       these are the read-only view's original values, unchanged. */
    #taskDetailDialog .tdd-body { margin: 0; padding: 20px 24px; max-height: 82vh; overflow: auto; }
    /* Tighter chrome in edit mode: the padding that frames a page of
       prose is wasted around a form. */
    #taskDetailDialog.is-editing .tdd-body { padding: 16px 20px; max-height: 88vh; }

    #taskEditForm label { display: block; min-width: 0; }

    /* Three columns. Two left the four short controls stacked over four
       rows with a hint under each, which is what produced the scrollbar. */
    #taskEditForm .tef-grid {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
        gap: 10px 14px;
        align-items: start;
    }
    #taskEditForm .tef-span2 { grid-column: span 2; }

    #taskEditForm .tef-check { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 8px; }
    #taskEditForm .tef-check input { margin-top: 2px; flex: 0 0 auto; }
    #taskEditForm .tef-check .tef-h { margin-top: 0; }

    #taskEditForm .tef-l {
        display: block; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600;
        color: var(--fg-secondary); margin-bottom: 3px;
    }
    #taskEditForm .tef-r { color: var(--danger-700); font-style: normal; margin-left: 2px; }
    #taskEditForm .tef-h {
        display: block; font-size: 11px; color: var(--fg-muted); margin-top: 3px; line-height: 1.3;
    }

    /* Control size is NOT reduced to make things fit -- padding and font
       size are the same as every other form in the product. The height
       came out of the column count and the spacing. */
    #taskEditForm input[type="text"],
    #taskEditForm input[type="date"],
    #taskEditForm select,
    #taskEditForm textarea {
        width: 100%; padding: 6px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
        border-radius: var(--radius-sm); font: inherit; font-size: 13px;
        /* Normal weight: AdminLTE makes every <label> bold (700) and `font: inherit` carried that weight into the control inside it (2026-10-26). */
        font-weight: 400;
        color: var(--fg-strong); background: var(--bg-surface);
    }
    /* Sized here rather than with a rows attribute so the two textareas
       stay equal and the short-viewport rule below can shrink them. */
    #taskEditForm textarea { resize: vertical; height: 76px; }

    /* A disabled control here means a governed field the rules do not let
       this task change -- the hint underneath always says which rule. */
    #taskEditForm input:disabled,
    #taskEditForm select:disabled { background: var(--bg-subtle); color: var(--fg-muted); }

    /* The action row stays put, so Save and Cancel are reachable even on
       a viewport short enough that the fields above have to scroll. */
    #taskEditForm .tef-actions {
        position: sticky; bottom: 0; background: var(--bg-surface);
        display: flex; justify-content: flex-end; gap: 8px;
        margin-top: 12px; padding-top: 10px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    }

    /* Two columns on a narrower window, one on a small screen. Below each
       breakpoint the extra column cramps rather than helps. */
    @@media (max-width: 1100px) {
        #taskEditForm .tef-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
    }
    @@media (max-width: 760px) {
        #taskEditForm .tef-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
        #taskEditForm .tef-span2 { grid-column: span 1; }
    }
    /* On a short viewport the textareas give up height first -- they are
       the only controls with room to spare. */
    @@media (max-height: 800px) {
        #taskEditForm textarea { height: 58px; }
        #taskEditForm .tef-grid { gap: 8px 14px; }
    }

    /* 482: recurring evidence rows on Complete Task. The radios are the
       shared .radio-group / .radio-option (cacca-styles.css); they only
       need to wrap inside the dialog's width. */
    #taskCompleteDialog .rw-evidence-source { flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px 16px; margin: 6px 0; }
    #taskCompleteDialog .tce-row {
        border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-md);
        padding: 8px 10px; margin-top: 6px;
    }
</style>

@*
    Complete Task — a workflow action, not a field.

    sp_task_complete enforces the BRD §12 mandatory-child gate, stamps
    completed_by / completed_dt, and emits ChildCompleted plus
    ParentEligibleForCompletion on the parent. None of that is what
    "set status = Completed" would do, which is why this is not a value
    in the Edit form's status dropdown.

    Small and confirming, per the requirement: this is a decision, not
    data entry.
*@
<dialog id="taskCompleteDialog" style="max-width:520px; width:94%;">
    <form id="taskCompleteForm" method="dialog" style="margin:0; padding:18px 20px;">
        <h2 style="margin:0 0 10px; font-size:16px;">Complete task</h2>
        <p id="taskCompleteSubject" style="margin:0 0 10px; font-size:13px; color:var(--neutral-700);"></p>
        <div id="taskCompleteGate" style="display:none; font-size:12px; border-radius:var(--radius-md); padding:8px 10px; margin-bottom:10px;"></div>
        @* 526: who the task goes to on Complete, when it has a reviewer / approver. *@
        <div id="taskCompleteReviewNote" style="display:none; font-size:12px; border-radius:var(--radius-md); padding:8px 10px; margin-bottom:10px;
                                               background:var(--primary-50); border:1px solid var(--primary-200); color:var(--primary-700);"></div>

        @* Evidence, as part of the completion workflow.
           Shown so the completer can see what is already attached, with
           the option to add more before confirming. NOT required: no
           per-task evidence-required flag exists (evidence_required lives
           on workflow_checklist_item, not practice_task) and
           sp_task_completion_eligibility does not consult evidence, so
           blocking completion on a file would be a rule this product does
           not have. *@
        @* 482: the recurring evidence of a scheduled task's obligation (moved
           off Operationalize by 481). Each row asks how it is provided --
           Direct Upload / Evidence Center Reference / External Evidence
           Reference -- and shows only that option's control. Optional:
           the 473 gate that required a file was removed by 482. Chosen
           files and external references are saved when the task is
           completed; Select from Evidence Center links at once. Hidden for
           any task that has no recurring evidence. *@
        <div id="taskCompleteRecurringWrap" style="display:none; margin-bottom:10px;">
            <div style="font-size:12px; font-weight:600; color:var(--fg-secondary); margin-bottom:2px;">Recurring evidence for this occurrence</div>
            <span style="display:block; font-size:11px; color:var(--fg-muted);">
                Optional. Choose how each one is provided. A chosen file or an external reference is saved when you complete the task.
            </span>
            <div id="taskCompleteRecurring"></div>
        </div>

        <div style="margin-bottom:10px;">
            <div id="taskCompleteEvidenceLabel" style="font-size:12px; font-weight:600; color:var(--fg-secondary); margin-bottom:4px;">Evidence</div>
            <div id="taskCompleteEvidence"></div>
            @* 483: the same three options as the recurring rows above. The
               radios are drawn by task-actions.js (Shared/evidence-source.js);
               each panel below shows for its option only. Select from
               Evidence Center links at once; Direct Upload stores the file
               when its dialog is submitted (499); the external reference is
               saved when the task is completed. The panels carry no inline
               display so [hidden] can hide them. *@
            <div id="taskCompleteGeneral">
                <div id="taskCompleteGeneralSource"></div>
                @* 499: was a bare file picker, which put the file in the
                   Evidence Center with no title, type, validity,
                   classification, tags or owner. The button opens the SAME
                   Upload evidence form the Evidence Center screen uses
                   (Shared/evidence-upload.js), so it is described once,
                   here, and stored on submit rather than at completion. *@
                <div data-ev-src-panel="DirectUpload">
                    <div style="display:flex; gap:8px; align-items:center; margin-top:6px;">
                        <button type="button" class="pm-button" id="taskCompleteUpload" style="padding:3px 10px; font-size:12px;"
                                title="Upload a file and describe it for the Evidence Center in one step.">
                            <i class="fa-solid fa-upload" aria-hidden="true"></i> Upload evidence
                        </button>
                    </div>
                    <span id="taskCompleteUploadNote" style="display:block; font-size:11px; color:var(--fg-muted); margin-top:3px;">
                        Optional.
                    </span>
                </div>
                <div data-ev-src-panel="EvidenceCenter" hidden>
                    @* 477: link evidence already in the Evidence Center. *@
                    <button type="button" class="pm-button" id="taskCompletePick" style="padding:3px 10px; font-size:12px; margin-top:6px;"
                            title="Link evidence already uploaded to the Evidence Center. It must be valid for this task's period.">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-box-archive" aria-hidden="true"></i> Select from Evidence Center
                    </button>
                </div>
                <div data-ev-src-panel="External" hidden>
                    <div style="display:flex; gap:8px; flex-wrap:wrap; margin-top:6px;">
                        <label style="flex:1 1 180px; font-size:12px;">Location
                            <input class="pm-input" type="text" id="taskCompleteGenLocation" maxlength="500"
                                   placeholder="Where it is kept" style="width:100%; font-size:13px;" />
                        </label>
                        <label style="flex:1 1 180px; font-size:12px;">Locator
                            <input class="pm-input" type="text" id="taskCompleteGenLocator" maxlength="500"
                                   placeholder="Path, link or reference" style="width:100%; font-size:13px;" />
                        </label>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div data-ev-src-panel="EvidenceCenter" hidden>
                    <span style="display:block; font-size:11px; color:var(--fg-muted); margin-top:3px;">
                        Optional. Linking is immediate and append-only &mdash; evidence is never
                        overwritten or deleted, so a newer item is added alongside the old one.
                    </span>
                </div>
                <div data-ev-src-panel="External" hidden>
                    <span style="display:block; font-size:11px; color:var(--fg-muted); margin-top:3px;">
                        Optional. The reference is saved when you complete the task.
                    </span>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <label style="display:block;">
            <span style="display:block; font-size:12px; font-weight:600; color:var(--fg-secondary); margin-bottom:3px;">Completion remark</span>
            <textarea class="pm-input" id="taskCompleteRemark" rows="3" maxlength="4000"
                      style="width:100%; font-size:13px;"
                      placeholder="What was done? Optional, but it is what the audit trail will carry."></textarea>
        </label>
        <p id="taskCompleteMsg" style="margin:8px 0 0; font-size:12px; color:var(--danger-700);"></p>
        <footer style="display:flex; justify-content:flex-end; gap:8px; margin-top:14px;">
            <button type="button" class="pm-button" data-close-task-complete>Cancel</button>
            <button type="submit" class="pm-button primary">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check" aria-hidden="true"></i> Complete task
            </button>
        </footer>
    </form>
</dialog>

@*
    Close Task — shutting a task WITHOUT completing it.

    sp_task_close carries no mandatory-child gate and writes no
    completion record. It is the "superseded / duplicated / no longer
    relevant" path, and the reason is required here because a closure
    with no completion needs one to be readable later.
*@
<dialog id="taskCloseDialog" style="max-width:520px; width:94%;">
    <form id="taskCloseForm" method="dialog" style="margin:0; padding:18px 20px;">
        <h2 style="margin:0 0 10px; font-size:16px;">Close task</h2>
        <p id="taskCloseSubject" style="margin:0 0 10px; font-size:13px; color:var(--neutral-700);"></p>
        <div id="taskCloseWarn" style="display:none; font-size:12px; border-radius:var(--radius-md); padding:8px 10px; margin-bottom:10px;
                                      background:var(--warning-50); border:1px solid var(--warning-200); color:var(--danger-700);"></div>
        <label style="display:block;">
            <span style="display:block; font-size:12px; font-weight:600; color:var(--fg-secondary); margin-bottom:3px;">
                Reason<span style="color:var(--danger-700);">*</span>
            </span>
            <textarea class="pm-input" id="taskCloseReason" rows="3" maxlength="1000" required
                      style="width:100%; font-size:13px;"
                      placeholder="Why is this being closed without completing it?"></textarea>
        </label>
        <p id="taskCloseMsg" style="margin:8px 0 0; font-size:12px; color:var(--danger-700);"></p>
        <footer style="display:flex; justify-content:flex-end; gap:8px; margin-top:14px;">
            <button type="button" class="pm-button" data-close-task-close>Cancel</button>
            <button type="submit" class="pm-button primary">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-lock" aria-hidden="true"></i> Close task
            </button>
        </footer>
    </form>
</dialog>

@*
    Reopen task — brings a Closed / Inactivated task back to Open.

    Mirrors the Close dialog. A reason is required and recorded in the
    state-transition history (reason_code TASK_REOPENED). The API
    (sp_task_reopen) authorizes admin OR the task owner; the menu item
    only appears on tasks whose current status is Closed.
*@
@*
    Review / Approve (migration 526). The reviewer or approver of a
    completed task approves it (on to the approver, or closed) or returns
    it to the assignee with a reason. sp_task_review_decide decides who
    may act; the dialog only shows whose turn it is.
*@
<dialog id="taskReviewDialog" style="max-width:560px; width:94%;">
    <form id="taskReviewForm" method="dialog" style="margin:0; padding:18px 20px;">
        <h2 id="taskReviewTitle" style="margin:0 0 10px; font-size:16px;">Review task</h2>
        <p id="taskReviewSubject" style="margin:0 0 10px; font-size:13px; color:var(--neutral-700);"></p>
        <dl id="taskReviewFacts" style="margin:0 0 10px; font-size:13px;"></dl>
        <label style="display:block;">
            <span style="display:block; font-size:12px; font-weight:600; color:var(--fg-secondary); margin-bottom:3px;">
                Remark <span style="font-weight:400; color:var(--fg-muted);">(required to return)</span>
            </span>
            <textarea class="pm-input" id="taskReviewRemark" rows="3" maxlength="2000"
                      style="width:100%; font-size:13px;"
                      placeholder="Your review comments, or why the task is being returned."></textarea>
        </label>
        <p id="taskReviewMsg" style="margin:8px 0 0; font-size:12px; color:var(--danger-700);"></p>
        <footer style="display:flex; justify-content:flex-end; gap:8px; margin-top:14px;">
            <button type="button" class="pm-button" data-close-task-review>Cancel</button>
            <button type="button" class="pm-button" id="taskReviewReturn">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-rotate-left" aria-hidden="true"></i> Return to assignee
            </button>
            <button type="submit" class="pm-button primary" id="taskReviewApprove">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check" aria-hidden="true"></i> Approve
            </button>
        </footer>
    </form>
</dialog>

<dialog id="taskReopenDialog" style="max-width:520px; width:94%;">
    <form id="taskReopenForm" method="dialog" style="margin:0; padding:18px 20px;">
        <h2 style="margin:0 0 10px; font-size:16px;">Reopen task</h2>
        <p id="taskReopenSubject" style="margin:0 0 10px; font-size:13px; color:var(--neutral-700);"></p>
        <div id="taskReopenWarn" style="display:none; font-size:12px; border-radius:var(--radius-md); padding:8px 10px; margin-bottom:10px;
                                      background:var(--warning-50); border:1px solid var(--warning-200); color:var(--danger-700);"></div>
        <label style="display:block;">
            <span style="display:block; font-size:12px; font-weight:600; color:var(--fg-secondary); margin-bottom:3px;">
                Reason<span style="color:var(--danger-700);">*</span>
            </span>
            <textarea class="pm-input" id="taskReopenReason" rows="3" maxlength="1000" required
                      style="width:100%; font-size:13px;"
                      placeholder="Why is this closed task being reopened?"></textarea>
        </label>
        <p id="taskReopenMsg" style="margin:8px 0 0; font-size:12px; color:var(--danger-700);"></p>
        <footer style="display:flex; justify-content:flex-end; gap:8px; margin-top:14px;">
            <button type="button" class="pm-button" data-close-task-reopen>Cancel</button>
            <button type="submit" class="pm-button primary">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-rotate-left" aria-hidden="true"></i> Reopen task
            </button>
        </footer>
    </form>
</dialog>

@*
    Add Evidence — the pre-completion path.

    Evidence often has to be attached BEFORE completion, for review or
    verification, so upload cannot live only inside Complete Task. It is
    its own small action, reachable from either page's action menu at
    any point while the task is open.

    It is not part of the Edit form either: Edit is an all-or-nothing
    transactional save of task fields, while an upload is multipart,
    immediate and append-only. A validation failure elsewhere in that form
    would roll back the fields and leave the file — so they stay separate.

    Append-only is deliberate. sp_task_attachment_add is the only writer;
    there is no delete and no replace, because evidence you can quietly
    remove is not evidence. Attaching a newer file adds it alongside, and
    both keep their own uploader and timestamp.
*@
<dialog id="taskEvidenceDialog" style="max-width:640px; width:94%;">
    <form id="taskEvidenceForm" method="dialog" style="margin:0; padding:18px 20px;">
        <h2 style="margin:0 0 10px; font-size:16px;">Add evidence</h2>
        <p id="taskEvidenceSubject" style="margin:0 0 10px; font-size:13px; color:var(--neutral-700);"></p>

        <div id="taskEvidenceExisting" style="margin-bottom:10px;"></div>

        <label style="display:block; margin-bottom:8px;">
            <span style="display:block; font-size:12px; font-weight:600; color:var(--fg-secondary); margin-bottom:3px;">
                File<span style="color:var(--danger-700);">*</span>
            </span>
            <input type="file" id="taskEvidenceFile" required style="font-size:12px; width:100%;" />
        </label>
        @* 477: or link evidence already in the Evidence Center. *@
        <div style="margin:0 0 8px;">
            <button type="button" class="pm-button" id="taskEvidencePick" style="padding:3px 10px; font-size:12px;"
                    title="Link evidence already uploaded to the Evidence Center. It must be valid for this task's period.">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-box-archive" aria-hidden="true"></i> Select from Evidence Center
            </button>
            <span style="font-size:11px; color:var(--fg-muted); margin-left:6px;">
                A file uploaded here is also kept in the Evidence Center for reuse.
            </span>
        </div>
        <label style="display:block;">
            <span style="display:block; font-size:12px; font-weight:600; color:var(--fg-secondary); margin-bottom:3px;">Description</span>
            <input class="pm-input" type="text" id="taskEvidenceDesc" maxlength="1000"
                   style="font-size:13px;"
                   placeholder="What does this file show? Recorded on the task's activity feed." />
        </label>

        <p id="taskEvidenceMsg" style="margin:8px 0 0; font-size:12px;"></p>
        <footer style="display:flex; justify-content:flex-end; gap:8px; margin-top:14px;">
            <button type="button" class="pm-button" data-close-task-evidence>Cancel</button>
            <button type="submit" class="pm-button primary">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-paperclip" aria-hidden="true"></i> Attach evidence
            </button>
        </footer>
    </form>
</dialog>

@*
    Migration 477: "Select from Evidence Center" on the Complete Task and
    Add Evidence dialogs uses the shared picker (_evidence-picker-dialog +
    Shared/evidence-picker.js, the Operationalize one). Included here, once,
    so every page that includes these dialogs gets it. pm-grid pages the
    picker's list.
*@
<partial name="Partials/_evidence-picker-dialog" />
<script src="~/js/pm-grid.js" asp-append-version="true"></script>
<script src="~/js/Shared/evidence-picker.js" asp-append-version="true"></script>
@* 482: the three evidence options, shared with Operationalize (481). *@
<script src="~/js/Shared/evidence-source.js" asp-append-version="true"></script>
@* 499: Direct Upload opens the Evidence Center's own Upload evidence form,
   so a file attached while completing a task arrives described rather than
   blank. Included here, beside the picker, so all four pages that render
   these dialogs (tasks / task-view / task-edit / task-complete) get it from
   one place. *@
<partial name="Partials/_evidence-upload-dialog" />
<script src="~/js/Shared/evidence-upload.js" asp-append-version="true"></script>
